quet of the Ten Virgins, in praise of purity.","athanasius":"Archbishop of Alexandria, the pillar of Orthodoxy against Arius; On the Incarnation.","ephrem":"Deacon of Edessa, the harp of the Spirit; hymns and homilies.","aphrahat":"The Persian Sage, the earliest Syriac Father whose writings we have.","basil":"Archbishop of Caesarea; On the Holy Spirit, the Six Days of Creation, the monastic Rules.","cyril-jer":"Archbishop of Jerusalem; his lectures prepared the newly baptised for the Mysteries.","nazianzen":"Archbishop of Constantinople, the Theologian; the Five Theological Orations.","nyssa":"Bishop of Nyssa, brother of St Basil; on the soul, the resurrection and the life of virtue.","macarius":"The Great, of Egypt: the Fifty Spiritual Homilies on prayer and the heart.","hilary":"Bishop of Poitiers, the Athanasius of the West; On the Trinity.","ambrose":"Bishop of Milan; on the Mysteries, the Holy Spirit, and the duties of the clergy.","chrysostom":"Archbishop of Constantinople, the Golden Mouth; homilies on the whole New Testament.","augustine":"Bishop of Hippo; the Confessions, the City of God and his homilies on the Psalms and St John.","cassian":"Brought the wisdom of the Egyptian desert to the West; the Conferences and the Institutes.","cyril-alex":"Archbishop of Alexandria; defended the Mother of God and the one Christ at Ephesus.","leo":"Pope of Rome; his Tome was received at Chalcedon: \"Peter has spoken through Leo\".","vincent":"Monk of Lérins: the faith \"believed everywhere, always and by all\".","gregory-dialogist":"Pope of Rome; the Pastoral Rule, the Dialogues and the Morals on Job.","isaac":"Bishop of Nineveh, the Syrian; on stillness, prayer and the mercy of God.","damascene":"Monk of Mar Saba; The Fount of Knowledge, with its Exact Exposition of the Orthodox Faith.","cyril-phil":"Equal-to-the-Apostles, Enlightener of the Slavs with his brother St Methodius; he defended the Holy Trinity before Muslim scholars at the caliph’s court.","abu-qurrah":"B